# CUSTOM. web/Dockerfile does `COPY . .` with this folder as the build context.
ops/
# ...except the container-start config script, which the production stage
# installs into /docker-entrypoint.d. It is the only thing in ops/ that belongs
# in an image; everything else there drives builds from the host.
!ops/runtime-config.sh

# EXCLUDE every host .env. The image is built with __HTTPSMS_<VAR>__ placeholders
# that the Dockerfile writes itself, and ops/runtime-config.sh substitutes real
# values at container start — so the build needs no configuration and must not
# pick any up.
#
# Excluding these is what makes the guarantee hold: nothing about this machine
# can reach the image, one artifact runs in dev and production, and a symlinked
# .env can no longer arrive dangling and silently bake upstream's
# api.httpsms.com into the bundle.
.env
.env.*

# Reinstalled inside the image; copying the host tree in is slow and can drag
# glibc-built binaries into an alpine build.
node_modules/
.output/
.nuxt/

# Not inputs to the build.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.example.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
*.superseded
